    "uid": "4fe8ba30de79b36de98679a5444fb7f9",
    "title": "File permissions weakened or locked",
    "desc": "A program changed a file's permissions in a way that is rarely routine - chattr toggling the immutable / append-only / undeletable attribute (locking a dropped webshell so it cannot be removed, or unlocking a protected system file so it can be tampered), or chmod making a file world-writable (777 / 666 / o+w / a+w). Weakening permissions is how an attacker leaves a file anyone can overwrite or read; locking one is how they protect their implant from cleanup (MITRE T1222.002). setuid_bit_set covers the setuid/setgid bit specifically; this covers the world-writable and immutable-attribute forms. An ordinary `chmod 644` / `chmod +x` is not matched.",
